title: barbarian_ritual
---
Narrator:
The system's moon is wrong.

---

Narrator:
It doesn't rotate. No tidal lock should produce this result at this orbital distance. Your navigator runs the calculation three times.

The moon is being held in place. Something is holding it.

---

Narrator:
On the surface, your long-range optics resolve shapes. Structures — no, formations. Living formations. Thousands of figures arranged in concentric rings around a central point.

They are performing something.

---

Narrator:
Your science officer says the readings from the central point are anomalous. Not impossible, technically. But anomalous.

She uses that word the way people use it when they don't want to say what they actually think.

---

-> [Allow observation — send a probe]
    <<apply_effect "eldritch_corruption">>
    Narrator:
    The probe transmits for eleven minutes before the feed cuts to static.

    Narrator:
    Your science officer seals the data. She says the probe's final images require further analysis.

    Narrator:
    Three crew members in the observation bay request medical leave. They won't say why.

    Narrator:
    Whatever is in that system, you've seen enough of it to know you don't want to see more.

-> [Destroy the formation — break the ritual]
    <<apply_effect "blessed_weapons">>
    <<chain_event "barbarian_relic">>
    Narrator:
    You fire from maximum range. The formations scatter.

    Narrator:
    The moon begins to rotate again.

    Narrator:
    Your weapons officer says the targeting systems felt "clean" during the engagement. More responsive. She can't explain it.

    Narrator:
    Something in that system approved of what you did.

    Narrator:
    That thought does not comfort you.

===
